From: mscharged-port
Subject: Keep the Wii widths of the flash API and declare C library calls natively
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility.

Decomp 9046e67a spells the nlFlash API and its users (SaveLoad, the file cache,
replays) with long and unsigned long, while nlFlash.cpp still defines it with
s32/u32/u8. On the Wii these are the same types; natively s32/u32 are 32-bit
and long may be 64-bit, so the header and the definitions disagree. Natively
the header declares the API with the source's own widths. The callbacks keep
their long result (a NAND result fits), and the five variables the API writes
a size or answer through are u32, as before upstream respelled them.

ODE's column and rounded-corner classes and the HOME button layout now take
sqrt and stricmp from MSL's internal/fdlibm.h and extras.h, which native
builds do not have on their path. Natively they keep the former extern "C"
declarations; the functions themselves come from the host C library (sqrt) and
the module's MSL extras.c (stricmp).

